  "scope": "One fresh Kubernetes v1.36.1 kind node and a dedicated Docker network attached only to that node and the fixture registry. A digest-pinned synthetic BusyBox image is pushed to a temporary authenticated loopback registry, pulled by kubelet into that node's cache, then challenged with imagePullPolicy Never under effective KubeletEnsureSecretPulledImages=true and AlwaysVerify. The no-identity Pod must remain container-free with ErrImageNeverPull; a Pod with the exact same synthetic registry identity must reuse the cached digest without registry manifest/blob access. IfNotPresent checks both approved reuse and a rejected registry fallback. An independently imported private fixture also needs successful registry authorization before reuse. Provider configuration, rotation, revocation, multi-node behavior and weaker policies are outside the case.",
